    issue('matrix-invertibility',[3,4,8],'K_e andK_c are explicitly symmetric positive definite. N2 only bounds conditional covariance bySigma_w and does not explicitly assumeSigma_w is invertible. Functional5 usesSigma_w inverse, so its ordinary formula requires positive definiteness or a separately supplied extension. ForSigma_w=0 admissible noiseless observations exist but that formula is undefined; no pseudoinverse convention is stated. T_xi itself may be rank deficient; positiveOmega regularizes its information matrix whenSigma_w is positive definite.')
    issue('radius-and-open-feasible-set',[4,8,9],'The ellipse display usesvarrho but its following prose saysradiusR. No positive-radius condition is explicit in the two theorem sentences; strictOmega>0 under trace<=varrho² requiresvarrho>0. Atvarrho=0 the parameter set is{0} while the strict feasible matrix set is empty. Preserve this endpoint limitation. The open feasible set need not attain its supremum; Section2.1 explicitly discusses approximating sequences.')
    issue('geometry-and-order',[4,8],'Error is measured withK_e, parameter norm withK_c inverse, and trace budget withK_c inverse square roots. The matrix products cannot be reordered by assuming commutativity. The estimator output need not lie inTheta. Theorem2 halves the radius, notK_c, the noise variance, or the constant alone.')
    issue('expectation-location',[8,10],'Omega is deterministic and selected before averaging overxi. Phi uses expectation of the inverse information-plus-precision matrix, not inverse of the mean information matrix;17 is a different lower bound. T_xi has no moment/rank assumption in the general setup, so17 may require extended-value/integrability interpretation. For the well-defined positive-definite noise case, the inverse in5 is bounded in PSD order byOmega, keepingPhi finite under its trace budget.')
    issue('proof-restrictions',[9,21,22,23],'Conditionally linear estimators, Gaussian noise reductions and prior constructions serve proofs and discussion. They do not narrow the all-measurable estimator class or theN1/N2 noise class in3. The auxiliary setK on22 permitsOmega semidefinite despite positive-definite prose; do not substitute it directly into5 with an ordinary inverse.')
    issue('finite-versus-infinite',[3,9,10],'The two theorem formulas use finite n-by-d matrices. Infinite-dimensional sequence/RKHS and IID/covariate-shift models are separate applications via approximation, not assumptions of both general Theorems. In particular, conditional noise bounds do not imply an IID sampling law.')
